## 14. Metrics That Matter (And Ones That Don't)

**Real signal:**
- Weekly installs from VS Code Marketplace (not cumulative).
- GitHub stars trend (3-day moving average).
- Issues opened by people who are not the author.
- Discussion threads in repo Discussions.
- Cold inbound emails / DMs asking about the project.

**Vanity metrics — ignore:**
- Total GitHub stars (look at the slope, not the total).
- HN frontpage position (only useful for the 24 hours it lasts).
- Twitter likes.
- "Time on page" or any analytics on the landing page.

**Real failure signals (act on these):**
- People install the Base extension, open the sidebar, see "no captures yet" forever, uninstall within 5 minutes. Reason: capture heuristic is too strict. Drop minInsertionLines to 2 and watch retention.
- Lite quickstart fails on Windows / WSL2 because of Docker compose v1 vs v2 differences. Fix the script.
- People email asking how to make it work with Cursor's agent mode. Answer: it can't, here's why. Don't promise what you can't deliver.

